Every binary this project distributes is listed below, because the installers
ship more than the server does and a notice that named only `pkgreg` did not
describe what a customer actually receives.

  pkgreg           the server
  pkgcache         the single-machine cache — the daemon and the CLI
  pkgcache-docker  the docker-compatible shim
  pkgcache-app     the desktop app
  pkgreg-client    the client installer   } standard library only; they link no
  pkgreg-bridge    the loopback bridge    } third-party module at all

The lists are derived from the linked module set — `go version -m` on each built
binary, and `go list -deps` for the platform builds that cannot be produced on
one host — not from go.mod, so they name what is actually distributed rather than
what is merely required for development or testing.

`pkgcache` and `pkgcache-docker` link the same set as `pkgreg`. `pkgcache-app`
links that set plus the app's own, marked [app] below; three of those are
platform-specific and are marked with the platform that links them.

